{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And you shall put into the breastplate of judgment the Urim and the Thummim.</b> It mentions them with the definite article, and it did not mention them in any place until now, for it did not enumerate them with the rest of the utensils in the labors of the craftsmen, so as to say concerning them 'and you shall make the Urim and the Thummim' as it says concerning the rest of the utensils, or that it should say 'and he made the Urim and the Thummim.' Now this is testimony that they were not the work of a craftsman but the work of Heaven. And because of this they were mentioned in the language of definiteness, in the manner of (Genesis 3:24) ״וישכן מקדם לגן עדן את הכרובים״ — and the cherubim were not mentioned previously; thus wrote the Ramban, of blessed memory. The general principle of the Urim and Thummim is that they were holy names, by whose power the priest knew the future and would declare to every questioner the things to come. These names had two aspects: the first — by their power the letters of the tribes fixed in the stones of the breastplate would light up, and these are called Urim ('lights'), in that they illuminated before the eyes of the priest; the second — by their power it would enter the heart of the priest that he should know to join and combine the letters and bring forth the word from them, so that he would hit upon the answer to the question; and by the power of these names the heart of the priest was whole (תמים) in knowledge of the letters, and through the holy spirit that was upon him it would enter his heart how they were joined and ordered, and these are called Thummim. And these two aspects of the holy names, called Urim and Thummim after their function, were placed between the folds of the breastplate, for that is why it was folded; and after Moses dressed Aaron in the ephod and the breastplate, afterward he would place between the folds of the breastplate the Urim and the Thummim, which is what is written: ״וישם עליו את החשן ויתן אל החשן את האורים ואת התומים״. This matter was one of the rungs of the holy spirit, above a bat kol and below prophecy. And they said at the beginning of the first chapter of Berakhot: Why are they called Urim and Thummim? Urim — because they illuminate their words; Thummim — because they complete their words. And they were also called Kreti and Peleti: Kreti — because their words are decisive (כורתין); Peleti — because their deeds are wondrous (מופלאין). And one who came to inquire of the priest through the Urim and Thummim — this was the procedure: the priest would stand with his face toward the Ark, and the questioner would stand behind the priest, and he would not ask in a loud voice nor would he merely ponder in his heart, but like a person who prays privately to himself, and he would utter the matter with his lips. And immediately the priest would be clothed in the holy spirit and gaze at the breastplate and see in it, like the appearance of prophecy, 'go up' or 'do not go up,' through letters that protruded from the breastplate opposite his face. And only a public body or a king may inquire, as is stated in tractate Sotah."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:19.155365967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}